-Romagna Region, in the middle of northern Italy. Visitors are drawn to Modena by its art treasures: the 12th-century cathedral and masterpieces of Italian Romanesque art, that together with the Piazza Grande and the Ghirlandina tower, create a complex of unique beauty, included by UNESCO in the \"World Heritage list\".","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Modena","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Modena","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Modena, in Italy, puts a UNESCO World Heritage Site and a serious food reputation in one compact centre. The Ghirlandina and Duomo di Modena lead, with Galleria Estense next. Ten hours covers it, and April, May and September are the best months.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":184732,"visit_h":7.3}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-modena-cathedral","name":"Modena Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":44.64623,"lon":10.92572,"dist_km":0.1,"rank_score":11.51,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-piazza-grande","name":"piazza Grande","kind":"Square","lat":44.64592,"lon":10.92561,"dist_km":0.1,"rank_score":7.43,"resolved_by":"retyped"},{"id":"hl-galleria-estense","name":"Galleria Estense","kind":"Museum","lat":44.64825,"lon":10.92066,"dist_km":0.4,"rank_score":7.22,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-museo-enzo-ferrari","name":"Museo Enzo Ferrari","kind":"Museum","lat":44.65216,"lon":10.9362,"dist_km":1.0,"rank_score":6.7,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/A_workshop_of_dreams_%2832354654116%29.jpg/960px-A_workshop_of_dreams_%2832354654116%29.jpg","author":"Pedro from Maia (Porto), Portugal","licence":"CC BY 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_workshop_of_dreams_(32354654116).jpg","w":3696,"h":2448,"ok_print":true}}],"do":[{"name":"Duomo, Ghirlandina and Piazza Grande","type":"activity","detail":"Cathedral, tower and square are one UNESCO listing. The Romanesque cathedral was 